{"comment":"The host page between the frame of a view and air-ide. The frame speaks MCP Apps (SEP-1865) by postMessage, with the extension x-air-app that it offers in appCapabilities. The host page maps each x-air-app message to the page link, and it keeps the order of the WebSocket. A runner of the host page serves the host document and plays air-ide on http://127.0.0.1:${port}, sends the lines of the frame and of air-ide, and checks its own: the ends host and page. The step pageLoad {url, location} loads the host document with ${ticket} in the fragment and expects the address of the page after it, without the ticket; pageShow {frame, theme} is the call window.airAppHost.show({frame, theme}) of the IDE after the load, which mounts the frame of the view once; pageTheme {theme} is setTheme(theme) after a change of the theme of the IDE; pageTicket {ticket} is connect(ticket), which gives the loaded page ${t2} after a drop."}
{"step":"pageLoad","url":"http://127.0.0.1:${port}/#ticket=${ticket}","location":"http://127.0.0.1:${port}/"}
{"step":"pageShow","frame":"https://fixture.air-genui-app.local/main","theme":{"dark":true,"values":{"background":"#1e1f22","foreground":"#dfe1e5"}}}
{"step":"wsHandshake","origin":"http://127.0.0.1:${port}","host":"127.0.0.1:${port}","expect":101}
{"link":"page","from":"page","message":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"channel":"ahp-root://","protocolVersions":["1.0.0"],"clientId":"page","ticket":"${ticket}","_meta":{"x-air-app":{"version":"1.0.0"}}}}}
{"link":"page","from":"air-ide","message":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"1.0.0","serverSeq":0,"snapshots":[],"serverInfo":{"name":"air-ide"},"_meta":{"x-air-app":{"version":"1.0.0","view":{"app":"fixture","view":"main","instance":"main:1","params":{}}}}}}}
